Z||000000||Pontiatic||10-12-2001||08:02 PM||||Since I've started driving to school I've had guys calling my car a "mini-Ferrari" or "mini-Lamborgini" I'm not quite sure why but it got me thinking. Has any Fieroite ever stuffed a Ferrari or other such exotic powerplant into a Fiero?||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||08:12 PM||||Not into, but around.  The fiero is a common platform for fiberglass rebodies... specifically Ferrari's (308/328, 355, Testarossa/512TR, and F50s) and Lambos (Countach & 25th anniv, and Diablo). Most of these rebodies (aside from the 308/328) require a frame stretch anywhere from 3" (F355) to 12.5" (diablo). Hence his term "Mini-Ferrari"  or whatever he calls it.  Also, many (uneducated) people associate the general appearance of a Fiero with a Ferrari (as well as the name).<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiatic||10-12-2001||08:38 PM||||yea i've seen the body kits to make them look like the ferrari's and coutaches(sp?) but im talkin pure italian power!||||reg||1
